{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_djmlttiaa4xmalhw2of3q6gx5npn7je3bxgx7yrwnsjzi6frojvq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What was done\n\n**Restructured the crate** so the translation can be verified through the FFI boundary. `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` only declares an executable, so I compiled the same untouched translation unit as a `.so` and made the Rust crate emit a matching `cdylib`:\n- `src/lib_impl.rs` — the translation, with `#[repr(C)]` structs and `#[no_mangle]` exports for all 15 library functions\n- `src/lib.rs` — the `cdylib`, adding the C-ABI `main` export\n- `src/main.rs` — the `driver` executable, pulling `lib_impl` in via `#[path]` (so one copy of the code serves both targets and the `main` symbols don't clash)\n\n**Phase A** — `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md` (54 rows + 9 generic boundaries), `CONFIGS.md` (91 rows). Only **one** build configuration exists: no `[features]` in `Cargo.toml`, no `option()`/`#ifdef` in the C.\n\n**Phases B–D** — 148 tests that `dlopen` **both** `.so`s with `libloading` and compare return values, stdout, stderr, and the full 256-byte `data` + `length` + `checksum` of every buffer. `nm -D` diff reaches empty: all 16 C symbols exported by the Rust `.so`, nothing stubbed.\n\n## Five real divergences found and fixed\n\n1. **`buffer_split` aliasing** — C computes `remaining = src->length - split_pos` *after* writing `dst1->length`. With `dst1 == src` that write clobbers `src->length`, so C yields an empty `dst2`; the translation had hoisted the read and produced 188 bytes.\n2. **`process_buffer_array` negative `count`** — C only rejects `count == 0`, so a negative count makes every loop body unreachable and returns 0. The translation's `count as usize` turned that into a ~2^64-iteration loop.\n3. **Exported `read_buffer` used `std::io::stdin()`** — whose buffer is a process-wide singleton, so read-ahead leaked across calls. Reader and writer now own their buffers over raw fd 0/1, like C's `FILE`.\n4. **`copy_nonoverlapping` on aliased args** — aborted where C's `memcpy(p,p,n)` is benign; switched to `ptr::copy`.\n5. **`init_buffer_array` pre-zeroed storage** — C leaves it uninitialized; zeroing made `capacity = INT_MAX` attempt a 584 GB memset instead of just failing the malloc.\n\n## Caveat worth flagging\n\nFor `length > 256`, five C helpers `memcpy` through a `uint8_t temp[256]` with no check — genuine UB (stack/struct overrun). The Rust clamps there to stay memory-safe rather than reproducing the overflow, and those inputs are excluded from differential execution; this is documented in `ERRORS.md` and is unreachable from the program, since `read_buffer` (the only way the executable populates a buffer) rejects `length > 256`.\n\nBeyond the cargo suite, the release executables were fuzzed against the cmake-built C binary for ~9200 additional randomized stdin streams with 0 mismatches."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":857,"cache_read_input_tokens":297679,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":857,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c2099b2-a280-4612-a6c0-406af3d1d538","uuid":"abcab29b-d27d-48ec-89ec-305e42b0121a","timestamp":"2026-08-19T22:54:23.484Z"}
